01 plan-writer done [12.8m 96 turns $4.29 · opus · default]: The plan (581 lines) covers renaming yourself on a new /settings page, display names unique across CollabHub regardless of case, and a 12/24-hour clock stored as a preference in Auth (D28 🟢, new D46). Auth gets a unique index on lower(display_name), which is the only thing deciding uniqueness. A rename to a taken name gets a 409, and a first sign-in with a taken name moves to `X 2`, `X 3`… inside savepoints, so it is never refused. Migration 0002 cleans and de-duplicates existing names before creating the index. Preferences are merged in one SQL statement, so two tabs writing different keys don't lose each other's change. The SPA gets a Settings page, a success handler that updates the user's own sidebar and every cached member directory (it still runs after the page unmounts, as checked in the installed TanStack 5.101 source), a clock that all three time formatters read, and a return to /settings after sign-in. That last one isn't there today: the issue assumed it was, and the plan records this as a correction. The recommended test approach is BDD with one journey: Alan renames himself, and Grace sees the new name after a reload. Everything else is unit, integration and Vitest, each test listed with the reason it fails before the code exists. 15 decisions are marked assumed: Postgres lower() not doing full Unicode case folding, which characters are refused, how an IdP name is cleaned, saving the same name being a no-op, how the migration handles reserved and deleted names, the return-to-path, where the page sits and what Back to chat goes to, the client-side validity check, 12/24 hours via hourCycle, and the preferences cache not being cleared on sign-out.
